OHOS: the editor has a dedicated recognition-result export entry point that
cannot reuse plain screenshot-save, because an authorized document URI must
be staged before the UIAbility copies it, and an HTML/Markdown export with a
companion .txt file needs a second authorization or the companion is
silently lost. Keeps its own cancellation id, QPointer and generation guards
against a stale callback writing into a newer request; the nested-callback
shape is this two-stage transaction's actual implementation, not incidental
complexity to simplify away.

